             'the exception).\n'
             '\n'
             'When a matching "except" clause is found, the exception is '
             'assigned to\n'
             'the target specified after the "as" keyword in that "except" '
             'clause,\n'
             'if present, and the "except" clauseâ€™s suite is executed. All '
